# LeakSanitizer suppressions.
#
# For leaks in code awlib does not own -- a system library that allocates
# once and never frees, a driver, an interpreter's global state. A leak in
# awlib itself belongs in a bug report, not in here.
#
# Syntax:  leak:<substring of a function name, file name or library name>
# Docs:    https://github.com/google/sanitizers/wiki/AddressSanitizerLeakSanitizer

# Lua keeps its allocations until lua_close(), which the bindings' tests
# deliberately skip in the cases that check error paths.
#leak:liblua
